&lt;ul data-start=&quot;30&quot; data-end=&quot;1477&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1senxlu&quot; data-start=&quot;306&quot; data-end=&quot;536&quot;&gt;Design, develop, and optimize LLM-based solutions, including model design, fine-tuning, deployment, and application of techniques such as prompt engineering, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and agent-based architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;2h1ju7&quot; data-start=&quot;537&quot; data-end=&quot;738&quot;&gt;Own and maintain high-quality, scalable, and efficient codebases in Python (using frameworks such as LangChain/LangGraph) and SQL, ensuring reusability, performance, and best engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;11mqx7&quot; data-start=&quot;739&quot; data-end=&quot;912&quot;&gt;Drive cloud integration and deployment of GenAI applications on platforms such as Azure, AWS, or GCP, ensuring efficient resource utilization and robust CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1mdrm5m&quot; data-start=&quot;913&quot; data-end=&quot;1111&quot;&gt;Collaborate closely with product managers, data scientists, and business SMEs to gather requirements, translate business needs into technical solutions, and deliver impactful AI-driven products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;so0eis&quot; data-start=&quot;1112&quot; data-end=&quot;1271&quot;&gt;Provide technical leadership, mentorship, and guidance to the engineering team, promoting best practices in machine learning and generative AI development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1ndxban&quot; data-start=&quot;1272&quot; data-end=&quot;1477&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;Stay updated with the latest advancements in LLMs and generative AI, proactively experimenting with emerging techniques and incorporating innovations to improve model performance and system capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1swn4yk&quot; data-start=&quot;240&quot; data-end=&quot;423&quot;&gt;8+ years of experience in&amp;nbsp;software engineering, or solutions engineering, ideally in a customer-facing capacity, including at least 2+ years focused on building and deploying AI/ML models and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1swn4yk&quot; data-start=&quot;240&quot; data-end=&quot;423&quot;&gt;1+ year of experience developing Generative AI (LLM) applications using techniques such as prompt engineering, RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), and/or agent-based frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;15gm1gz&quot; data-start=&quot;424&quot; data-end=&quot;556&quot;&gt;Strong expertise in architecting and designing GenAI applications and systems using modern frameworks and cloud-native services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;egl7sn&quot; data-start=&quot;557&quot; data-end=&quot;676&quot;&gt;Proficiency in working with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP to build, deploy, and scale GenAI solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;bq55o6&quot; data-start=&quot;677&quot; data-end=&quot;780&quot;&gt;Strong programming skills in Python, along with hands-on experience in LangChain/LangGraph and SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;o3t16s&quot; data-start=&quot;781&quot; data-end=&quot;884&quot;&gt;Proven ability to lead and drive engineering teams toward execution of a defined technical roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;8xfvop&quot; data-start=&quot;885&quot; data-end=&quot;1036&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with business SMEs and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s, Master&#39;s, or Ph.D. in &lt;strong&gt;Computer Science&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$180-220K Base + equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are client first&lt;/strong&gt;: We put our clients at the center of everything we do, because their success is the ultimate measure of our value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We work at Start-Up Speed: &lt;/strong&gt;We move fast, stay agile and favor action because momentum is the foundation of perfection&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are AI forward: &lt;/strong&gt;We help our clients build the future of Al and implement it in our own roles and workflow to amplify productivity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advantages of joining Turing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Amazing work culture (Super collaborative &amp;amp; supportive work environment; 5 days a week)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Awesome colleagues (Surround yourself with top talent from Meta, Google, LinkedIn etc. as well as people with deep startup experience)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet every single qualification.&amp;nbsp;Turing is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;At Turing we are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive and authentic workplace&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;and celebrate authenticity, so if you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;For applicants from the European Union, please review&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.turing.com/policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Turing&#39;s GDPR notice here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

forerunnerventures-glossier:greenhouse:7.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Glossier is a people-powered ecosystem, brought to life by engaging online and offline experiences. In 11 years, we have built an iconic brand that goes far beyond beauty. Our brand is built on trusted emotional connection, empathy, and consistency in how we show up for people every day. We are woven into everyday moments of people’s lives, becoming part of their routines, their self-expression, and their confidence. We are defined not just by what we make, but by how we make people feel and the relationships we build over time. &lt;strong&gt;Our north-star values are to be Human, Curious, Playful, and Helpful. &lt;/strong&gt;We are driven by a shared mission to become the Most Loved Lifestyle Brand in the World.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE FORMULA.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We’re looking for a Vice President, Product to help shape what’s next at Glossier and bring it to life in a way only we can. Think of this role as a carefully crafted formula: equal parts visionary and operator, with a strong dose of curiosity, taste, and follow-through. We’re looking for someone who can see what’s coming, translate it into products our community will love, and meaningfully involve that community as a source of inspiration, insight, and co-creation throughout the development process, leading the work from idea to shelf and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the CEO, the VP, Product will set the direction for our product portfolio across multiple categories, building an innovation roadmap grounded in consumer insight, cultural relevance, and market opportunity, and expressed through a lens that feels fresh, distinctive, and unmistakably Glossier. This leader will partner closely with Marketing, Creative, Supply Chain, Quality, and Finance, and play a key role on the Senior Leadership Team to ensure cross-functional alignment, clarity, and momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is all about balance: instinct and analysis, big-picture vision and rigorous execution, brand-building and business-driving. You will define our long-term product vision, create a differentiated pipeline of innovation, and ensure every product we bring to market meets a real customer need– while aspiring to create the next generation of category-defining, iconic products that only Glossier can deliver. Just as important, you’ll build and lead a high-performing Product team, fostering collaboration, elevating standards, and ensuring best-in-class work at every stage of the process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The North Star: Build iconic, category-defining products &lt;em&gt;with&lt;/em&gt; our community, not just for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re energized by building, refining, and reimagining, and know how to pair creativity with disciplined execution, you may be exactly the ingredient we’re missing. So, is this you? Read on carefully to see what it takes to bring this vision to life from start to finish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BRINGING IT ALL TOGETHER.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;From bringing new ideas to life (and reimagining what already exists), shaping the future of our portfolio, to leading and inspiring the team behind it all, the Vice President, Product will play a key role across &lt;strong&gt;Product Development &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Product Strategy &amp;amp; Portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Product Development &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end product development lifecycle, driving decisions across formulation, claims, naming, pricing, testing, and production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver best-in-class launches across new products, reactivations, and renovations, from concept through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute the product roadmap, ensuring on-time, on-budget delivery to the highest quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and scale standardized processes for PD/PM collaboration, including clear briefs and decision frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop innovation pipelines informed by consumer insights, community feedback, and industry trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed community-driven insights into product briefs and portfolio decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure rigorous validation of product claims, safety, stability, and compatibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and strengthen relationships with contract manufacturers and external partners to accelerate development cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead reformulations, repackaging, and optimizations to enhance competitive positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support international expansion, including reformulations for compliance, localized claims, and registrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Strategy &amp;amp; Portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define long-term portfolio strategy to drive differentiation and global growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead 3-year category planning and portfolio strategy across Skincare, Makeup, Body Care, and Fragrance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reporting frameworks to assess category health and portfolio performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop data-driven business cases for new launches and product investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead consumer research and concept testing to validate innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and scale key marketing levers, including promotions and reactivations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Creative and Brand Marketing to deliver impactful launch strategies and assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own global pricing strategy, balancing customer experience, competitiveness, and margin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing Product team, fostering innovation, accountability, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own PD/PM budgets, forecasts, and alignment with Finance on revenue goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with cross-functional leaders across Supply Chain, Operations, Brand, and Creative to drive execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion efficient, standardized ways of working to accelerate timelines and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support key retail partnerships, including Sephora, in collaboration with Wholesale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage budgets, timelines, and cost targets to support growth and profitability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve on the Senior Leadership Team and act as a key partner to Founder &amp;amp; Executive Chairwoman Emily Weiss&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY INGREDIENTS.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We know you’re here to do great work, raise the bar, and make a meaningful impact, and we’re here for that, too. While there’s no single path to success, we’ve found that the key ingredients below set the foundation for doing your best work, thriving in the role, and ultimately making it your own (i.e. successfully bringing this formula to life).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience across product development, portfolio strategy, and/or product marketing within beauty or adjacent consumer categories, including 4+ years in senior leadership roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and bringing differentiated product pipelines to market at global scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading end-to-end product development, from concept and formulation through commercialization and launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong vendor management experience (domestic and international)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and analytical thinker with strong attention to detail; able to balance big-picture portfolio strategy with tactical execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator and presenter, comfortable with executives and large groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and collaborating with cross-functional teams including regulatory, marketing, operations, and supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep passion for beauty, with strong creative instincts and a willingness to take thoughtful risks that reflect customer needs and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as needed to meet with vendors or external partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In accordance with the applicable law, the following represents a good faith estimate of the minimum and maximum compensation range for this position:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;The estimated annual pay range for this role is $235,000.00 - $305,000.00 per year.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation will be determined based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to the candidate’s experience, skills, qualifications, and location, and the final offer will reflect the totality of the candidate&#39;s background.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;There may be future opportunities for continued pay progression based on continued strong performance in the role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Full-time positions are also eligible for a competitive compensation and benefits package that include medical health insurance, 401K, equity in the form of Restricted Stock Units, Paid Time Off, Short Term and Long Term Disability leave, and a range of other benefits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Learn more at the&lt;a href=&quot;https://life.glossier.com/&quot;&gt; Glossier Career page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Compensation for the role will be determined based on permissible, non discriminatory factors such as a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://life.glossier.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Click here to view the candidate privacy policy under FAQ&#39;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an Equal Employment Opportunity (“EEO”) Employer. It has been and will continue to be a fundamental policy of Glossier not to discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, marital status, partnership status, domestic violence victim status, sexual orientation, age, national origin, alienage or citizenship status, veteran or military status, disability, medical condition, genetic information, caregiver status, unemployment status or any other characteristic prohibited by federal, state and/or local laws. This policy applies to all aspects of employment, including hiring, promotion, demotion, compensation, training, working conditions, transfer, job assignment, benefits, layoff, and termination.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
